At the age of 20 Njoud adopted her first dog a Labrador named Ace and he was her inspiration to realize her true calling of becoming a professional dog trainer.

After the amazing success she had training her own dog she started working with different organizations and shelters along side a mentor trainer, which gave her the opportunity to gain experience and knowledge working with different breeds and backgrounds. She rescued, fostered, and trained many dogs along the years then adopted her other dog Karaz.

Njoud wanted to expand her knowledge and skillset so she attended and graduated from Animal Behavior College as a dog trainer. She developed her skills and methods with the help of her mentor and continued to study Training Shelter Dogs, Canine Diet & Nutrition, Pet Massage,  and Pet CPR & First Aid. 

Njoud has experience working on private lessons, board and train, group classes, and behavioral modification. She is committed to continuing education and always looking for opportunities to learn and grow. Her purpose in life is to give each dog the fulfilled and healthy life they deserve',true,'{}'::text[]) on conflict (id) do nothing;

