My background includes working with military K9s, explosive detection K9s, and search and rescue K9s, ensuring dogs are highly skilled and reliable in high-stakes environments. I’ve also trained service dogs to assist individuals with disabilities, conservation K9s for wildlife and environmental protection, and protection K9s for security purposes.
Beyond specialized working dogs, I have extensive experience rehabilitating shelter dogs, giving them a second chance at life, and training pet dogs to become well-mannered companions. My diverse expertise allows me to tailor training programs to fit any dog’s needs, whether for work, service, or home life.
As a nationally certified Trainer, Instructor, and Explosive Detection K9 Handler, I combine proven techniques with real-world experience to deliver results. My mission is to help every dog reach its full potential while strengthening the bond between dog and owner through clear communication, trust, and consistency.
I believe that dogs are more than just animals—they are family. Every dog I work with is treated with love, respect, and compassion. My goal is not only to train dogs but to help build stronger, lifelong relationships between dogs and their owners.',true,array['Address conflict: your list 93635, sheet 93265']::text[]) on conflict (id) do nothing;
Work: 321-914-5917','915 N 198th St, Shoreline, WA 98133','Seattle','WA','98133',47.7377,-122.3431,'Driving range: 50 miles',50,4,12,'All programs','All programs',null,'Jahrony','XXL',null,'Helping Hands  425-672-4343 18415 33rd Ave W, Ste R  Lynnwood, WA, 98037','Blue Pearl  (206) 624-9111 805 Madison St Seattle, WA 98104','Shelby Hunziker - Friend 3213618404','2025-12-16','Like many of my clients, I owned a dog that had behavioral issues but there wasn’t a dog trainer in my local area that could help me. I had adopted a young, female bully breed that matured into a dog with severe dog on dog aggression. Dog trainers in my home town weren’t equipped with the knowledge about behavior modification. So, I began doing my own research and working with my dog, Honey, to help her cope with a world that was filled with dogs. After a few failures but many successes, Honey was able to reach a level of advanced obedience and off leash reliability. We were often able to seamlessly move throughout crowds at dog friendly events without worry but I stayed vigilant and advocated for Honey’s personal space. This is where my passion for dog training was born.

The knowledge that I gained was further put to work when rescues, my local shelter and a dog rehabilitation farm began asking for help with their dogs. This helped me garner some unique experience that I still use in my daily dog training. Soon, I was under the apprenticeship of a local dog training company that eventually led to my employment as the lead dog trainer and behavior specialist of my local SPCA dog shelter. Through working at the shelter, I was forced to think of unique solutions for dog training in that high stress environment. With doing that, I was able to successfully place many dogs with a multitude of behavioral challenges into life-long homes. I also provided after adoption dog training support and helped to reduce the return or surrender of countless dogs.

I bring many years of dog training experience with me and a specialization in aggressive behavior and situations that need delicate or complex solutions. I have a judgment free, positive attitude and when it comes to aggressive behaviors, I’ve been there and done that! While I love watching the transformation of my challenging dog training clients, I also enjoy training all breeds for obedience and helping owners live happily with their pets!',true,'{}'::text[]) on conflict (id) do nothing;
